==Battleground==
*1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**8 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
**5 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is a big step-up from the previous one. Far more enemies spawn, including multiple Shadow Boxer K's. Dark Otter is very bulky and there are multiple of them in the level, although they don't push quite as hard as the other enemies in the stage.

You should bring [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]], such as [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|The Flying Cat]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO]], and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris/Cyborg Cat]] to handle the rush of enemies after hitting the base and damage the Dark Otters. 3 or more meatshields can hold off their advance, while a stronger unit like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] is also highly recommended for additional damage against the Dark Otters or Shadow Boxer K's.

